WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.640
That's enough!

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.900
Thank you very much!

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.560
Rinka-san!

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.040
They have new flavors at the creperie by the station.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.910
Let's go together!

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.620
The three of you should go and have fun.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.120
Are you going to train again?

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.880
How about taking a break every now and then?

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.630
Sorry.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.520
Rinka-san is working so hard every day...

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.510
Good job!

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:44.250
I heard they have new flavors at the creperie by the station!

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.190
Let's go together!

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.360
I...

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.870
Come on, let's go Rinka-chan! Hurry!

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.660
W-Wait, Nami-san.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.160
These feelings that I couldn't even tell my friends about

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.490
are still locked up inside me even now

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:17.580
If I eat the magical fruit inside my heart

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:22.550
they might actually be able to come out

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.160
I kept on waiting in the classroom

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.160
making excuses that it's just a coincidence

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.750
That smile is probably meant for someone

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.210
If dreams can make my wishes come true

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:49.160
I want to give you this present

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:54.330
I will transform your rainbow

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:59.290
into a bridge of happiness, just wave to me

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:04.570
It's all right, it's all right

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:09.920
I simply want to watch over you...

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:28.080
<i>At the Closed Place</i>

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.540
A Tomato Special this morning?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.540
Very luxurious.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.060
Yeah, well...

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.300
I received a lot of them from Tama-nee.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.920
You say that... but in truth you went out and bought them for me, didn't you?

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.160
Why would I do that for you!?

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.270
That's... well...

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.690
Well, I guess you're right.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.030
It's nothing to go to such lengths for.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.530
Of course not.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.070
You wouldn't be that attentive to me in the first place, would you?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.160
What's that supposed to mean!?

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.400
Well, excuse me for being attentive to you at times!

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.260
Which is it...?

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.700
Geez... if this keeps up we'll never be able to make up.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.660
The Gift's summer is already over, huh!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.240
The real summer will come soon enough.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.170
No thanks.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.750
Don't be reserved!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.250
Huh?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.360
But... I cannot have you do this...

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.770
It's fine!

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.980
You're my Rinka-chan after all!

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.770
Hey, what's up?

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:04.760
Sempai...

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:05.920
Who are you?

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.020
What? We met at the beach, didn't we?

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.300
Really?

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.520
Well, whatever.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.270
<i>This girl really needs to get off her high horse!</i>

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.630
Rinka-chan, you're so amazing!

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.210
You've been training all morning, haven't you?

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.780
Yes... well...

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:25.660
That's why I'm going to support you!

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.660
I stayed up all night making you a lunch!

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.720
Come on, dig in!

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.690
That doesn't look bad.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:39.500
I'll have one!

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:40.760
Sempai!

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.450
Where are your manners!?

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:52.520
Rinka-chan, eat up before someone pinches it again!

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.600
It's delicious, isn't it!

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.820
Those cooked pears are what I'm most proud of!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.050
I'll have one too!

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.040
Delicious!

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.040
Eat all you want!

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.720
What are you doing?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.000
That lunch tastes bad enough to make me barf!

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.300
That food isn't edible to human beings!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.720
I'll make you a lunch every day from now, okay?

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.040
Err, don't you think that's a bit...

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:32.680
What!?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.050
Well, you see...

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.300
Every day...

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.520
She won't be able to go on a date with her boyfriend!

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.020
Rinka-chan doesn't have a boyfriend!

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.030
Isn't that right, Rinka-chan?

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.510
You don't have a boyfriend, do you?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.530
Do you?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.580
I do!

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:55.250
That is him!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.760
I am truly sorry!

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.760
I blurted it out without thinking...

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.560
Well, that lunch isn't really something one can live through.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.020
I understand how you feel, Rinka.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.900
I'll be your lover.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:23.520
I'm saying that I'll go out with you.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.110
What are you trying to pull?

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.610
Idiot, we're just pretending!

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.870
I'm telling her I'll pretend to be her boyfriend!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.170
Oh.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.450
That's it!?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:38.990
However, I cannot trouble you that much...

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.160
Then are you gonna eat that lunch every day?

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:44.960
I am counting on you!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:47.970
Come.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:49.920
Umm...

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.340
Nami's watching.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.180
Excuse me.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:05.320
By the way, are you free this Sunday?

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.280
Yes.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.030
My training will finish in the morning.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:12.050
Then how about we go out at noon?

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.310
A date?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:20.400
If we want to convince Nami, we'll at least have to go on a date or two!

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.620
I... guess.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.710
Understood.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.040
"Eek!"

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:27.650
"Bump."

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:28.460
"Squeeze."

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:30.830
"Hey, watch where you're going!"

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.840
"You're surprisingly well endowed."

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.390
"W-What a thing to say after bumping into me!"

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:40.480
<i>Monthly Rubon</i>

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.900
"Oh... he bought a kitten."

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.480
"He might actually be kindhearted."

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.130
"Badump."

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:43.820
"What is this feeling?"

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.450
"H-Hey, wait!"

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.560
"What is it?"

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:52.060
"I... I always thought you were a stupid and rude guy."

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:52.660
"Huh?"

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.410
"But still, I... love you!"

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.870
But still, I... love you!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:04.480
What should I do!?

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.220
I could never say something like this!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.550
Good luck on your date tomorrow.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.170
Why do I get left-overs?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.980
Hey, you're early!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.030
Did you wait long?

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.530
Please take care of me today!

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.760
S-Same here...

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.160
That sounded a bit stiff...

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.600
I apologize.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:40.960
Well, let's go.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:41.910
Yes.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.360
Hey...

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.420
Isn't this kinda embarrassing?

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.660
But, on a date you...

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:58.270
You don't even see this in girls' comics anymore.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.460
No, I read about this last night!

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.810
W-What is this feeling?

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:14.400
I-I always thought... you were a stupid and rude guy.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.490
H-Hey, what are you saying all of a sudden!?

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.410
Stop it!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.160
But still, I...

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.410
...lo... lov...

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.990
Rinka, I beg of you, please stop!

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:26.500
...love you!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.920
Stop it!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.570
Sorry about yesterday.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.930
It's okay.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:40.560
So it's a lie that you're dating!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.780
Nami-san.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:47.970
I've been watching you all day yesterday.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.800
You weren't acting like lovers at all!

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:52.280
Th-That is...

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.050
Why?

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.110
Why would you lie about that?

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.280
Do you hate me that much?

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.850
No.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.240
That is not it...

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:03.040
It is just that I...

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.690
Hey, lay off a bit, will you?

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.300
Have some understanding for her fee—

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.770
I want to be together with Rinka-chan!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:29.310
In the first year of the Genji era (1864)...

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:33.360
...after receiving rewards for their valor during the Ikedaya incident...

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.860
...Itou Kashitaro joined the ranks of the Shinsengumi...

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.500
Why?

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.040
Why can't I be with Rinka-chan?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.040
Why...

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:54.440
The Shinsengumi, who participated in the battle of Toba-Fushimi...

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:56.730
Hokazono, pay attention.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.300
I am sorry.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:05.810
I... want to be with Rinka-chan.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:09.500
Rinka-chan... feels that way too, right?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:22.890
Hey!

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:24.740
Sempai...

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:28.360
Umm...

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:29.210
About today...

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.810
I know.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.250
Our "lovers" plan failed big time.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.430
Yes...

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:36.630
Thank you for everything.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.720
I have club activities now, so...

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.340
Okay. See ya.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.970
Too bad you can't be her mock boyfriend anymore.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:51.150
Well, I can't help it.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.560
Oh really?

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.670
Things haven't been going very smoothly.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:04.780
Huh?

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:06.740
S-Sempai?

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.630
Why are we in the hallway...?

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.540
What's going on?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.330
We just went outside, didn't we?

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.480
Yeah...

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.630
Let's try opening this door again.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.880
Hold it!

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:19.920
Edo-kun?

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.240
An abnormal phenomenon has befallen this school.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:31.980
What do you mean?

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.100
Let me explain.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.310
Basically...

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:41.320
...this.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.950
I can see how it's a dangerous situation.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.130
At present, space inside the building has been distorted...

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.250
...allowing passages between places that could normally never exist.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.210
We have to determine the location of origin.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.250
Come!

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:58.880
This is reconnaissance unit...

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.540
...Mr. Scout!

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:03.210
Switch on!

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.970
Go!

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.470
Investigate the cause of the space distortion!

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.470
Scout!

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:12.690
Oh well.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.810
Never letting yourself be discouraged is one of the fundamentals of science.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.810
Failure is indispensable while in pursuit of the truth.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:23.320
So in short, the distortion of space was what caused that thing to come back from behind us?

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:28.030
This phenomenon has transformed the school into something akin to a labyrinth.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.400
Remodeling complete.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.620
Go! Mr. Scout Mk. II!

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:39.670
Time to go!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.720
Wh-What are you guys doing here!?

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.220
Looks like we can't go outside...

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:59.700
And I was planning on cheering on the shopping district's baseball team...

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:01.860
I see... that's too bad.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:09.290
Captain told me he would hit a hundred homeruns for me.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:10.780
That's impossible!

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.540
What's going on here!?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.650
Why on earth...?

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.870
I don't know the reason.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.380
However, the cause is...

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.370
Yes, no doubt about it.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:28.720
It's Gift.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.970
A notification by the student council.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:38.420
Until we have assessed the situation, please do not move from your current location.

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:42.730
This is all the Gift's fault again.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.350
What should we do?

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.320
Our cell phones won't connect...

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:51.550
In emergency situations like these, the person in charge needs to keep their head cool!

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:52.990
Keep your cool!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.790
You need to keep cool!

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.660
Sorry...

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.580
I hate Gift...

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:05.420
Mr. Scout Mk. IV has halted.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.800
The center of distortion seems to be the Kendo dojo.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.720
So that's where the person who tried to send this Gift is...

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.340
Who could it be?

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.360
Nami-san.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:20.900
Nami-san was always watching me there.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.570
Men!

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:24.440
Ippon!

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:25.940
It's over!

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:29.990
Rinka-chan, awesome!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.570
I want to be together with Rinka-chan!

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:37.790
That is why...

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.440
Those feelings...

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:44.790
Her one-sided feelings brought forth a deflected Gift...

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>Onii-chan...</i>

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.440
The space distortion is destabilizing.

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:56.260
What?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:16:00.900
The space that had been forcefully distorted seems to be rebounding.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.380
It's truly interesting.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:04.270
Is this the time to be calm!?

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.570
Riko!

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:26.960
Onii-chan!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.160
Hurry!

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.390
Are you okay, Riko?

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.020
You didn't get hurt?

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.220
No, I'm fine.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.230
But you, your hand!

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:47.190
This is nothing.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.020
No!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:56.870
Man, you do some crazy things sometimes.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.270
Can't you say it a little nicer?

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.520
I'm complimenting you.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.100
Oh really?

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.120
Sempai.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.170
I am going to see Nami-san.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.370
Wait!

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:10.050
I have some responsibility in this as well.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.590
But...

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.050
I cannot trouble everybody any more...

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:14.990
Then let's go together.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:17.900
Maki, lend me the radar.

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:18.650
Here.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:23.890
Just follow Mr. Scout Mk. IV's signal to reach the Kendo dojo.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:24.940
Got it.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:25.960
Onii-chan...

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.480
It'll be fine. I'll be right back.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.240
Be careful.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:34.490
Shall we go, Rinka?

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:35.300
Yes.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.420
This way?

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:54.220
Hey, why are you trying to do everything on your own?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:59.090
Well, just don't be too hard on Nami.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.470
It's tough having to deal with unreciprocated feelings.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.900
Where's Nami?

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:16.650
Nami-san!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.490
It's me, Rinka!

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:21.190
Nami-san, you are here, right?

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.690
Rinka-chan, so you came.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:27.750
Where is she?

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:31.250
I like you more than anyone, Rinka-chan.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:34.340
Rinka-chan, you like me too, right?

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:35.990
Isn't that right?

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.100
Right?

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:39.480
Right!?

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.790
Nami-san!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:41.850
Please listen to me.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:49.110
In my family, the Ousou sword style is passed on from generation to generation.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:53.280
And, in order to master this style...

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:56.650
...it takes two swordsmen to unite their strength.

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.760
Enduring severe training together...

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.560
...with their minds perfectly in line with each other.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.870
Two... swordsmen?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.540
I had a sister five years older than me.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.630
My sister was incredibly strong. I aspired to be just like her.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:18.840
Mastering the Ousou style together with my sister was my purpose in life.

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:20.250
But...

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.260
How pitiful...

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.810
She was still in high school...

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:27.600
What's going to happen to the Ousou style now?

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:30.560
Poor Rinka-chan, left all alone...

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.230
It's the end for the Ousou style.

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:37.570
To fulfill the will of my deceased sister...

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:41.570
...I vowed to continue practicing the Ousou style on my own.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.150
Without relying on anyone else.

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:47.870
Mastering the Ousou style... together with the soul of my sister.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.000
Rinka-chan.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.170
Am I not good enough?

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:56.090
I want to become your strength.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:20:01.720
To master this style, it is necessary to endure life-threateningly harsh training.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.100
Not you...

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:06.930
No... I cannot get anyone involved in that.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.020
I can handle it!

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:13.490
If it's for you, I can endure anything!

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:17.090
So... I want to be your number one!

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.060
Nami-san...

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:21.240
Hey, swordsman training isn't child's play!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.110
I'll work hard!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:25.280
If I'm with Rinka-chan, I know I can do it!

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:27.120
You...

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:31.510
You were great when you saved Riko-san earlier, Sempai.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.810
R-Really?

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.340
I kinda did that in a haze...

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:39.590
In a haze... huh?

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:43.550
As long as your feelings are strong enough, you can do anything.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.600
The training is very strict, you know.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.320
Rinka-chan!

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:50.560
I'm sorry...

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:51.780
I'm so sorry!

00:20:56.970 --> 00:21:02.280
Fight! Fight!

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:05.030
Hey! Keep in pace, everyone!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.780
Run faster!

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.440
Why are you giving orders!?

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.900
She's pretty cheeky for a newcomer.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.540
How annoying!

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.670
I'm Rinka-chan's number one, after all!

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:21.050
Let's race to the dojo!

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.420
Not so fast!

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:25.150
Looks like things have worked out.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.470
That's youth for you.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.010
You know the character for "person"...

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.770
...is like two people supporting each other, like this.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.520
Kirino-chan, until when did you have club activities again?

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:40.300
My piano was flooded, so I'll be free for a while.

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:43.720
Wanna go to the creperie at the station on our way back?

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:44.540
Okay!

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:48.780
Hey, you guys! Just when someone is letting you in on an interesting story!

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:51.110
Listen, the character for "love" is...

00:21:51.110 --> 00:21:52.020
I know, I know.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:54.450
It has the character for "heart" in its center, right?

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:55.780
You know!?

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:56.830
Of course!

00:22:12.090 --> 00:22:16.270
In a corner of the classroom

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:22.860
I hummed my favourite song

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:28.790
Why did those melancholic feelings

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:33.020
well up within me today

00:22:34.570 --> 00:22:40.060
When I return, will this town

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:43.850
gently welcome me back?

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:48.040
Hey, I want to meet you

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:55.160
In times you feel down, I wish you would tell me

00:22:55.160 --> 00:23:00.080
before you can no longer turn back

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:04.030
Building a heartfelt rainbow together

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:06.840
Say that I'm not alone

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:12.990
So that my prayers may be heard

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:35.180
Apparently, there are rumors floating around about a witch distributing fake Gifts.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:37.070
How outrageous.

00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:41.790
Only the power of science can make people's desires come true.

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:42.840
What's wrong, Amami?

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:46.930
You are seeing your mother in Fukamine-san?

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:51.940
Why do unscientific things keep occuring in this town!?

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:59.950
<i>Appearances</i>

00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:54.450
Next time, "Appearances."

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:58.500
Who will you give your Gift?
